    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> Using :first-child is very similar to :first-of-type but with one critical difference: it is less specific. :first-child will only try to match the immediate first child of a parent element, while first-of-type will match the first occurrence of a specified element, even if it doesn't come absolutely first in the HTML.\r\n\r\nSource: https://css-tricks.com/almanac/selectors/f/first-child/\r\n\r\nAngular probably creates some sub-elements making `:first-of-type` ineffective. We can use `:first-child`.",
    "commit_id": "530374e3f91b8f8f97510774b9bd3a7cf3895792",
